Cellular Biology and Genetics Study Guide

Cell Structure and Organelles:
The plasma membrane encloses the cytoplasm. Mitochondria generate ATP through cellular respiration. The cell nucleus contains chromatin and directs ribosomal transcription.

DNA Replication:
DNA replication occurs during the S phase of interphase. DNA helicase unwinds the double helix, while DNA polymerase synthesizes leading and lagging strands.

Protein Synthesis:
Transcription produces messenger RNA (mRNA) from a DNA template. Translation occurs at the ribosome where transfer RNA (tRNA) delivers amino acids based on codon sequences.

Mendelian Inheritance:
Gregor Mendel formulated the Law of Segregation and the Law of Independent Assortment using monohybrid pea plant crosses.
